From 30343a2ff9c00ee7a0e585cbdbd2f81b07ba9d58 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:05:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] gateway: a unit's `gateway run` child behind a
 wrapper ExecStart is a service gateway

hermes-worker-2 (2026-11-12): hermes-gateway.service runs hermes-gateway-broker
(token-broker exec ... -- github_quota.py ... -- hermes gateway run), so the unit's
MainPID is a wrapper and the gateway is its child. _get_service_pids returned only
MainPIDs, so `hermes update`'s post-update manual sweep mapped the unit's own gateway
(pidfile -> profile default) as a manual gateway: it armed a detached
`gateway run --replace` watcher and drained the unit's gateway. The relaunch ran in
hermes-core-update.service's cgroup and held the gateway lock, while the unit looped
on exit 75 (already_running, ~every 7.5 s, NRestarts 117+) and could not own it.

_get_service_pids now adds the `gateway run` descendants of each systemd unit's
MainPID (gateway_service_members.gateway_descendant_pids; non-gateway descendants
such as card workers are left out, so find_gateway_pids never reports them). Every
caller only uses the set to protect PIDs, so the manual sweep, survivor sweep,
stale-survivor restart, orphan reaper and inventory classifier all now treat the
child as service-managed.

_parse_ps_line and _iter_windows_list_processes move unchanged to
gateway_process_listing.py to keep gateway.py under its line cap.

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_gateway_service_child_pids.py (real wrapper process
tree; RED on main: both fail, GREEN with the fix).
